#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Catch the h287 defect class: Actor.fail() exiting the process before a
watch-mode Actor persists the baseline that already-charged rows are recorded in.

Cycles 676-680 found and fixed 4 live instances of this shape (fec-campaign-finance-
scraper, ats-jobs-scraper, trademark-search-scraper, eu-ted-tenders-scraper) by hand,
one grep-and-read pass at a time. No static check covered it -- this is that check.

Heuristic (textual, not a real control-flow analysis): for every Actor whose source
declares a `watchLabel` input (i.e. it persists a watch baseline via a
`saveWatchRecord(` call), find the LAST line that calls `saveWatchRecord(` and the
FIRST line that calls `Actor.charge(`. Any `Actor.fail(` call sitting between those
two lines can fire *after* a row has been pushed and charged for but *before* the
baseline recording that charge is saved -- exactly the shape that caused the re-charge
bug. An `Actor.fail(` before the first charge (e.g. input validation) is fine, since
nothing has been charged yet to lose the record of.

This does NOT prove a flagged call is reachable mid-run (vs. only ever firing before
any charge), only that the textual ordering is suspicious -- a cheap trip-wire, not a
substitute for reading the function and reproducing against the live API the way the
4 real fixes did. Two known false positives are ALLOWLISTed below: a purely textual,
line-number heuristic can't see that `Actor.charge(` sits inside a helper function
whose FIRST call site is actually later than a validation-time `Actor.fail(` earlier
in the file, or that a branch's own guard condition (e.g. "every pair failed, so this
run's push-count is provably 0") makes it safe. Read the allowlist reason before
trusting it -- it must name the invariant that makes the flag safe, not just silence it.

Exit 0 = clean, 1 = drift found. Usage: check-fail-ordering [slug ...]
"""
import os
import sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))

# (slug, 1-indexed line number of the Actor.fail( call) -> why it's safe despite the
# textual ordering. Re-verify the reason still holds if the line number ever shifts.
ALLOWLIST = {
    ("apple-podcasts-scraper", 1148): (
        "the h289 seed gate added cycle 696. It fires only when `seedErrors` is non-empty, "
        "and every push into `seedErrors` is itself wrapped in `if (seeding)` -- while "
        "seeding, the code records watch ids and `continue`s (line 632) without ever calling "
        "pushResult(), so a seed run's charge count is provably 0 and there is no charge "
        "record to lose. Re-verified cycle 1034 by re-reading the guard at its new location "
        "(still holds, no logic change): `if (watchMode && seedErrors.length) { await "
        "Actor.fail(...) } else if (watchMode) { await saveWatchRecord(...) }`, byte-identical "
        "condition to the cycle-986 re-verification. Line shifted from 1096 to 1105 -- cycle "
        "1030's search-dedupe double-charge fix (`pushedFromSearch.has()` check + a log.info "
        "line) added 9 net lines above it; no logic changed in the seed gate itself. Also "
        "spot-checked the other 3 `seedErrors.push(` call sites (lines 845, 1039, 1074): each "
        "sits in a fetch/search-failure branch where nothing was pushed for that item, "
        "consistent with the same invariant."
        "Re-verified cycle 1276 (still holds, line 1105 -> 1107, line shift only): the gate is byte-identical `if (watchMode && seedErrors.length) { await Actor.fail(...) } else if (watchMode) { await saveWatchRecord(...) }`, and all 3 `seedErrors.push(` sites (now 847, 1041, 1076) are still each gated `if (seeding)`, with line 634 still `if (seeding) { watchSeen.add(watchId); continue; }` so a seed run never reaches the charge at line 261."
        "Re-verified cycle 1416 (still holds, line 1107 -> 1148, line shift only, +41 lines from cycle 1414's work above it). This one surfaced as a LIVE FLAG rather than a silent pass -- the allowlist is keyed on (slug, line), so a shifted line does not silence a known-safe call, it re-flags it; that is the intended design (a moved call must be re-read, not auto-trusted) but it means the check reads `1 suspect` against its recorded `0` baseline until the key is updated. Gate still byte-identical: `if (watchMode && seedErrors.length) { await Actor.fail(...) } else if (watchMode) { await saveWatchRecord(...) }`. All 3 `seedErrors.push(` sites (now 888, 1082, 1117) are still each gated `if (seeding)`, so `seedErrors.length > 0` still implies `seeding === true`; line 675 is still `if (seeding) { watchSeen.add(watchId); continue; // baseline: record, never push/charge }`, so a seed run never reaches the sole `Actor.charge(` at line 302 and its charge count is provably 0."
    ),
    ("app-store-reviews-scraper", 933): (
        "input validation on the resolved `apps` list, fired before the app/country loop "
        "that ever calls Actor.charge( even starts -- nothing can have been charged yet. "
        "Re-verified cycle 845 (still holds): unchanged `if (!apps.length) await Actor.fail(...)` "
        "guard, no charge-capable code above it. Line shifted from 815 by cycle 845's watchEvents "
        "(scoreChanged) change, which added code before this point."
        "Re-verified cycle 996 (still holds, same guard condition read live in source); line shifted +21 by cycle 996's bare-date calendar-day window fix, which added lines in the input-parsing block only (nothing charge-capable)."
        "Re-verified cycle 1276 (still holds, line 928 -> 933, line shift only): same `if (!apps.length) await Actor.fail(...)` guard, and re-traced the helper-indirection claim rather than assuming it -- `Actor.charge(` is at line 361 inside `chargeAndPush`, reached only via `pushResult` (defined 393, called only at 849 inside `scrapeAppCountrySort`), and the first real call into that chain is `scrapeAppCountry(...)` at line 1046, i.e. 113 lines AFTER this fail. Nothing charge-capable executes before it."
    ),
    ("app-store-reviews-scraper", 1176): (
        "guarded by pairsAttempted > 0 and storefrontErrorPairs.length === pairsAttempted "
        "-- every pair in this run errored, so nothing was ever pushed/charged to lose. "
        "Re-verified cycle 845 (still holds, same guard condition read live in source). "
        "Line shifted from 1054 by cycle 845's watchEvents (scoreChanged) change."
        "Re-verified cycle 996 (still holds, same guard condition read live in source); line shifted +21 by cycle 996's bare-date calendar-day window fix, which added lines in the input-parsing block only (nothing charge-capable)."
        "Re-verified cycle 1276 (still holds, line 1167 -> 1176, line shift only): guard read live in source, unchanged `if (pairsAttempted > 0 && storefrontErrorPairs.length === pairsAttempted)`."
    ),
    ("app-store-reviews-scraper", 1192): (
        "guarded by pairsAttempted > 0 and feedServed === 0 -- nothing came out of Apple "
        "for any pair in this run, so nothing was ever pushed/charged to lose; comment in-code "
        "confirms this fires before the watch record write on purpose. Re-verified cycle 845 "
        "(still holds, same guard condition read live in source). Line shifted from 1070 by "
        "cycle 845's watchEvents (scoreChanged) change."
        "Re-verified cycle 996 (still holds, same guard condition read live in source); line shifted +21 by cycle 996's bare-date calendar-day window fix, which added lines in the input-parsing block only (nothing charge-capable)."
        "Re-verified cycle 1276 (still holds, line 1183 -> 1192, line shift only): guard is now `if (pairsAttempted > 0 && feedServed === 0 && !timeBudgetExceeded && await reviewFeedIsDown())` -- the `!timeBudgetExceeded` conjunct added since the last re-verification only NARROWS when the fail fires; `feedServed === 0` still proves nothing was pushed or charged."
    ),
}


def find_calls(lines, needle, exclude=None):
    out = []
    for i, l in enumerate(lines):
        stripped = l.strip()
        if stripped.startswith("//"):
            continue
        if needle in l and (exclude is None or exclude not in l):
            out.append(i)
    return out


def main(argv):
    wanted = set(argv[1:])
    drift = 0
    checked = 0

    actors_dir = os.path.join(ROOT, "actors")
    for slug in sorted(os.listdir(actors_dir)):
        if slug == "_template" or slug.startswith("."):
            continue
        if wanted and slug not in wanted:
            continue
        src = os.path.join(actors_dir, slug, "src", "main.js")
        if not os.path.isfile(src):
            continue
        with open(src) as fh:
            text = fh.read()
        if "watchLabel" not in text:
            continue
        lines = text.splitlines()
        save_lines = find_calls(lines, "saveWatchRecord(", exclude="function saveWatchRecord")
        if not save_lines:
            continue
        checked += 1
        last_save = max(save_lines)
        charge_lines = find_calls(lines, "Actor.charge(")
        first_charge = min(charge_lines) if charge_lines else None
        fail_lines = find_calls(lines, "Actor.fail(")
        if first_charge is None:
            suspect = []
        else:
            suspect = [
                i for i in fail_lines
                if first_charge < i < last_save and (slug, i + 1) not in ALLOWLIST
            ]
        if suspect:
            drift += 1
            rows = ", ".join(f"line {i + 1}" for i in suspect)
            print(f"{slug:33} SUSPECT Actor.fail() before last saveWatchRecord() (line {last_save + 1}): {rows}")
        else:
            print(f"{slug:33} ok (last saveWatchRecord() line {last_save + 1}, {len(fail_lines)} Actor.fail() call(s), 0 between first charge and save)")

    print()
    print(f"check-fail-ordering: {checked} watch-mode Actor(s) checked, {drift} suspect fail-before-save ordering(s)")
    return 1 if drift else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
